+// space transform, so FAAL has to run *before* that transform. We evaluate JSM's
+// PLAYER_TURN mapping here instead, filter those two scalars, and fold the result
+// back into the 3D vector.
+//
+// Both directions are homogeneous: the delivered yaw is linear in (Y,Z) and the
+// delivered pitch is linear in X, so multiplying (Y,Z) by s scales the game's yaw
+// by exactly s, and multiplying X by s_p scales its pitch by exactly s_p — without
+// having to replicate the game's math.
+// Three modes (FAAL_PSMOTION_MODE):
+//   0 OFF    — pass the calibrated gyro through untouched
+//   1 PLAYER — the game does its own player-space transform, so we only scale its input
+//   2 LOCAL  — the game reads local axes with no transform, so we run it for them
